{
  "_comment": "Rich Black LibreOffice settings manifest. Read by apply.py. Values that reference Theme.qml use 'token:<Name>'; literal colors use '#RRGGBB'. ColorScheme entries become decimal xs:int colors under /org.openoffice.Office.UI/ColorScheme/ColorSchemes/RICH_BLACK/<Entry>.",
  "simple_items": [
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.Common/Accessibility",
      "prop": "IsAutomaticFontColor",
      "type": "boolean",
      "value": true,
      "why": "CRITICAL readability fix: lets LibreOffice pick a readable font color automatically instead of the forced (invisible) one. Schema: main.xcd, org.openoffice.Office.Common group Accessibility, xs:boolean, default false."
    },
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.Common/Misc",
      "prop": "SymbolStyle",
      "type": "string",
      "value": "sifr_dark",
      "why": "Icon theme. 'colibre' (previous value) ships dark glyphs invisible on dark bars. 'sifr_dark' is the monochrome symbolic set with near-white (#efefef) glyphs; installed at /usr/lib/libreoffice/share/config/images_sifr_dark(_svg).zip. Schema: main.xcd, Common/Misc SymbolStyle xs:string ('auto'/'default'/theme name)."
    },
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.Common/Appearance",
      "prop": "ApplicationAppearance",
      "type": "short",
      "value": 2,
      "why": "Force dark chrome. Enum per LibreOffice UI (Tools > Options > Application Colors > Appearance: 0=System/Automatic, 1=Light, 2=Dark); schema main.xcd declares it as xs:short 'Application Colors'. Value 2 already present and observed dark; kept."
    },
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.Common/Appearance",
      "prop": "LibreOfficeTheme",
      "type": "short",
      "value": 1,
      "why": "THEME ENGINE SWITCH (fixes brown chrome + transparent menus). Enum per include/vcl/themecolors.hxx ThemeState: 0=DISABLED, 1=ENABLED, 2=RESET; schema main.xcd Common/Appearance LibreOfficeTheme xs:short default 0. At 0, ColorConfig_Impl::SetupTheme() returns early, ThemeColors never caches the registry scheme, and VclPluginCanUseThemeColors() is false, so the gtk3 backend ignores every ColorScheme chrome entry (FaceColor/MenuColor/...) and paints chrome+popups from system/GTK colors (brown, translucent). At 1 the RICH_BLACK chrome loads and menus paint opaque. Was 0."
    },
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.Common/Appearance",
      "prop": "UseOnlyWhiteDocBackground",
      "type": "boolean",
      "value": true,
      "why": "Keep the document page WHITE (WYSIWYG) even under a dark theme. Schema: main.xcd, Common/Appearance, xs:boolean, default true."
    },
    {
      "path": "/org.openoffice.Office.UI/ColorScheme",
      "prop": "CurrentColorScheme",
      "type": "string",
      "value": "RICH_BLACK",
      "why": "Select the custom RICH_BLACK application-color scheme defined below (built from Theme.qml tokens). Schema: main.xcd, org.openoffice.Office.UI group ColorScheme, CurrentColorScheme xs:string."
    }
  ],
  "color_scheme": {
